  "usage": "full landline number in national form (10 digits): 011-2345678, (081) 222 3456; drop a leading +94. A bare code is not accepted, so other countries' codes don't match",
  "note": "29 geographic codes named after the exchange town; a code's area does not follow district borders, so each key lists every district it reaches. Cross-border coverage checked against OpenStreetMap: about 1,580 Sri Lankan landline numbers from phone/contact:phone tags were placed in the 25 district polygons and counted by code; codes seen only on hotels, bank branches and chain head offices (e.g. 011 island-wide) were not counted, codes on local schools, councils, hospitals and shops were. Thin evidence (066 in Polonnaruwa, 091 in Matara, 054 in Nuwara Eliya) is left out.",
  "miss_note": "not a Sri Lankan geographic code: 07x mobile, or a code missing from the TRCSL list (e.g. 046, 060)",
  "source": [
